# {{project_name}} — SPRAG Labs

A showcase app that exercises SPRAG's framework primitives one
entry at a time. Each route is a focused demonstration of a single
Specter + Ragot feature, runnable in isolation.

The labs skeleton is a living regression canary: every entry that
scaffolds + builds + renders cleanly proves the primitive still
works end-to-end. Adding a new entry is the easiest way to stress
a specific slice of the framework.

The shared app chrome lives in `app/shell.html` and `app/shell.css`.
Individual routes and mounts can attach their own shell CSS without
copying the app frame into browser Components.

## Running

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
. .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
sprag dev --port 8000
```

Open <http://127.0.0.1:8000/>.

Optional env settings live in `.env.example`. Copy the keys you want into
`.env` or `.env.local`. Only `SPRAG_PUBLIC_` values are exposed to browser
Modules and Components.

## Entries

| Route              | Mode     | What it exercises                          |
|--------------------|----------|--------------------------------------------|
| `/`                | document | Landing — links to every entry             |
| `/counter`         | hybrid   | `@action` + `Module` + `Component` loop    |
| `/virtual-scroll`  | hybrid   | `@virtual_scroll` on a large list          |
| `/store-demo`        | hybrid | `store(...)` as flat cross-runtime state         |
| `/nested-store-demo` | hybrid | The same `store(...)` with nested path-style ops |
| `/queue-demo`        | hybrid | `QueueService` background work + SSE bus         |
| `/watcher-demo`      | hybrid | `Watcher` service broadcasts                     |
| `/operation-demo`    | hybrid | `Operation.run` success and failure paths        |
| `/form-demo`         | hybrid | `form_data(...)` + dirty state + redirect submit |
| `/form-demo/success` | document | publish redirect landing page                 |
| `/animation-demo`    | hybrid | `@animate` + `sprag.dom` animation helpers       |
| `/socket-demo`       | hybrid | `SocketIngress` + shared websocket bridge        |
| `/lifecycle-mount`   | mount  | SPA-style workspace mount + child teardown       |
